# Row, Row, Row Your Boat: traditional American round (words 1852; tune as published by E. O. Lyte, 1881).
{title: Row, Row, Row Your Boat}
{composer: Traditional (USA); tune Eliphalet Oram Lyte}
{key: C}
{tempo: 90}
{time: 6/8}
{x_level: 1}
{x_strum: D - - D - -}

{comment: Two downs per bar (1 and 4) to start; later try D - D D - D.}

{comment: Sing it three times. As a round, the next voice starts when the first reaches line 2.}

{start_of_grid label="Verse"}
| C . | C . |
| C . | C . |
| C . | C . |
| G . | C . |
{end_of_grid}

{start_of_verse label="Verse"}
[C]Row, row, row your boat,
Gently down the stream;
Merrily, merrily, merrily, merrily,
[G]Life is but a [C]dream.
{end_of_verse}
{x_end: C}
